# Results

table = Variant,Visitors,Conversions,Conversion rate,Lift vs control,p-value; Control (Place order),48210,1832,3.80%,none,none; Variant B (Complete purchase),48095,1919,3.99%,+5.0%,0.14; Variant C (Pay securely now),48302,2068,4.28%,+12.6%,0.003

# Conversion rate

data cr = variant,rate; Control,3.80; Variant B,3.99; Variant C,4.28

chart bar cr unit=% labels title="Conversion rate by variant"

# Daily trend

data daily = day,Control,Variant C; Sep 22,3.71,4.19; Sep 23,3.85,4.33; Sep 24,3.79,4.24; Sep 25,3.92,4.40; Sep 26,3.68,4.17; Sep 27,3.83,4.31; Sep 28,3.81,4.29

chart line daily x=day y=Control,Variant C unit=% title="Daily conversion rate, final week"

# Decision

! Ship Variant C to 100 percent of traffic.

Variant B was not significant, with a p-value of 0.14. Average order value did not change: it was $87.40 for Variant C and $87.15 for control.
